  "id": "osf-symlink-resolution",
  "generatedAt": "2026-10-07T12:35:04.123Z",
  "title": "Symlink resolution in osf check and scan",
  "summary": "Adds a shared `symlink` module that resolves links inside the repository to the real files behind them, and wires it into `osf check` (scan, lint-writing, lint-skill) and into the scan walker. Previously every symlink was skipped and counted as excluded; now an in-repo link is followed and its real files are scanned, while a link that points outside the repository, into `.git`, at nothing, or in a loop is refused with a `symlink refused:` error. Git-tracked mode is unchanged: tracked symlinks are still excluded rather than read.",
